    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Kyle Tucker**, who commands the highest daily efficiency score (81.11) due to a prime matchup against Merrill Kelly. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill projection and prime protection in the order, making him our top offensive pillar. **Andy Pages** (74.84) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) also present strong plays; **Andy Pages** capitalizes on the same favorable matchup against Kelly, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** gains significant value from a dynamic platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle. These players are currently our most reliable options to drive counting stats in today\u2019s 5x5 rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved the final utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (48.75) narrowly missed the cut behind lower-ranked but higher-floor starters. While **Miguel Vargas** holds a respectable xwOBA of 0.382, he was pushed out by the positional efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** (66.19), whose high SP skill boost against Chase Petty made him too valuable to bench in a category-scarcity environment. Managers should remain vigilant regarding the 38-40% rain risks affecting **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; if these games face delays or cancellations, we will need to pivot to bench depth. Additionally, **Gunnar Henderson** faces a moderate hurdle against Nathan Eovaldi, where his score is suppressed slightly by the pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners, a critical factor given our emphasis on stolen bases.",
